; The shop's zone, shop.test. Names without a final dot end in .shop.test,
; and @ is shop.test itself, the zone's apex. The SOA's numbers are the
; serial, refresh, retry, expire and minimum. Change a record, raise the
; serial, then: rndc reload shop.test
$TTL 300
@        IN SOA ns1.shop.test. hostmaster.shop.test. ( 2026111201 3600 600 1209600 900 ) ; serial
@        IN NS    ns1
@        IN NS    ns2
ns1      IN A     198.51.100.13
ns2      IN A     198.51.100.14
@        IN A     203.0.113.40
www      IN CNAME @
api  600 IN A     203.0.113.41
mail     IN A     203.0.113.42
status   IN A     203.0.113.43
@        IN MX    10 mail
@        IN TXT   "v=spf1 mx -all"
@        IN CAA   0 issue "ca.shop.test"
; The European site, eu.shop.test, is delegated to its own server, ns-eu.
; To delegate it, take the ; off the start of these three lines and fill
; in each ...: the server's name, its address (the glue), and the DS
; record of eu.shop.test's key.
;eu       IN NS    ...
;ns-eu.eu IN A     ...
;eu       IN DS    ...
